 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92cb42d6-33e7-5895-a2ef-8224d17bd632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} {:answer/id #uuid "bde6ef7f-70fd-5236-a1cb-ae7873bad5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cb42d6-33e7-5895-a2ef-8224d17bd632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469882} :answer-field/id #uuid "5757eb5a-153a-5404-853e-2408f7e8d9f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae6d946d-9a9f-5816-82c2-7048c4392f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-96857" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,-1),(-2,1),$ and $(3,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(1,3)$\n- **II.** $(0,-3)$\n- **III.** $(2,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-9),$  $(1,3)$, and $(3,9).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \" I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ea197e-9076-5ec7-9c6b-fde342e50e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452287} {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e5c9ca-6cc9-55d4-93e3-da3cb1057919" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b2c027-6043-5549-871e-78ddef1107d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} :answer-field/id #uuid "51370f87-3ad5-5a80-a161-072ee50a64dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} {:answer/id #uuid "1fac6913-2157-5d65-b290-ffccbb160d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53a4dc2-d964-58e2-b05c-d5768a79a4e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63a8e650-529a-5d09-8a67-87993316a8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97061" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463ae41e-390b-598e-ad2c-cc70f9b8b51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452293} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc1bf5b2-a5c1-5687-973d-01d75246fa11" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} {:answer/id #uuid "8a857a45-934f-59cb-806a-0ff39125394b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e95157d-1201-5d7b-96c1-63d2f59338ce" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82668a3d-f3fe-5542-b38c-eb8caa646e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452297} {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a201872-4c57-5d35-8831-ed55fb963e8f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47f484a7-fae0-59b3-b230-0181ae09e78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97064" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} {:answer/id #uuid "42f83495-bf79-5e40-bb79-ee3727fa8353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/