tion.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "977acc9f-1a7e-5840-a4f9-507f36de32d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-97065" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050324 :topic/id #uuid "3ffd42a4-cf3d-5ec4-9be0-19d427299cac" :topic/math-academy-id 2014 :topic/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} {:answer/id #uuid "22258483-ea45-5772-80af-642cced16361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} :answer-field/id #uuid "87d25a98-a59c-5918-a546-bfaab5b15f74" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e02f4008-99e6-55f7-ae03-99655f56fc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452307} {:answer/id #uuid "9b593e7d-bb2c-5419-b993-7de85e7d1b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b593e7d-bb2c-5419-b993-7de85e7d1b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452308} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4b4bc3-162c-5c39-b8fe-688b73fee26c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "863769ed-1b89-5bb8-8f85-696676c0d657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452309} {:answer/id #uuid "d6531f9e-30e6-57d5-98d6-0eb2d7c0a854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "863769ed-1b89-5bb8-8f85-696676c0d657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452309} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac9e825-f8fb-5632-a250-538164e4e4be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bdd43e6-c23f-5a39-9c12-13372eb04201" :question/math-academy-id "q-97066" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{B}=[T]_{C}^{-1}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{C}=[T]_{B}^{-1}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dbfc974-64a1-5ba8-a98a-3c44ced3256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452317} {:answer/id #uuid "4692bc9a-0874-5399-a418-98fb85a5cec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbfc974-64a1-5ba8-a98a-3c44ced3256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452317} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e47d84-f057-5e0a-ae70-ec0d33904e89" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420fa2b5-f5a7-5d27-bc3d-9bbf0b0cd31b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452319} {:answer/id #uuid "27f8b042-1a66-5c50-9a92-c6c664837fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f8b042-1a66-5c50-9a92-c6c664837fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452320} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e76e66-d34f-5c65-9093-a22e5839e130" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6839f-b647-50f5-9788-3ee7b2fa1f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452321} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4185c8-8f28-5d02-aeb6-193573874b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d6839f-b647-50f5-9788-3ee7b2fa1f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452321} :answer-field/id #uuid "883ab182-da38-5ef9-bdd1-6c14d39cea71" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2667e6b9-8784-550d-a849-0ee298d78d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-97078" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Im}(T)={0}$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The condition $\\text{rank}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/title "Linear Algebra: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549302} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550037}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9e07b5-9f0c-5f9e-b5e0-dd0bb5ddbb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452329} {:answer/id #uuid "d14bb30d-305a-547d-9203-a605f0933196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b9e07b5-9f0c-5f9e-b5e0-dd0bb5ddbb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452329} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e160ff3-065c-5657-8ce0-3c4b6d039613" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "818a42fb-6b7f-5df4-8ab0-b6fbd9ce9828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452331} {:answer/id #uuid "8e28d75e-6501-56ba-b2ec-7c348ccf4ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "818a42fb-6b7f-5df4-8ab0-b6fbd9ce9828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452331} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02af0b4-2c7a-5f06-8bce-9c46c66d51fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c808587e-3884-59ef-af9c-8252842bfe9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452333} {:answer/id #uuid "798caed6-3130-5378-93c1-4a0623b4f841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "798caed6-3130-5378-93c1-4a0623b4f841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452334} :answer-field/id #uuid "f055b1e5-126e-5f0a-bbc9-b574c36ec312" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b24ab75-1f17-54d0-bd60-01447f2e1769" :question/math-academy-id "q-97149" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the inner product in ${C}^{n}$ is linear in the first argument. So, a constant multiple from the first argument can be factored out.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac261e67-ef83-599b-9f7a-2f0221d53c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452335} {:answer/id #uuid "a8955430-a9ed-5bcb-ac12-138c73b1312a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac261e67-ef83-599b-9f7a-2f0221d53c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452335} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ce4c66-39b4-5114-9f3a-f7a49fb4749a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453015} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4385f63-a19e-59b3-b375-1f827b7a2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452337} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fb5fe-2a57-5b9f-8207-21687f865974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f93fb5fe-2a57-5b9f-8207-21687f865974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452338} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e2913a5-5b90-507c-ba81-c9f768ab74f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d2b1a3-de50-5a4d-8436-402d7d7ff9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452339} {:answer/id #uuid "80eb1877-a06a-52e2-9a0b-c6ad7075ac0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d2b1a3-de50-5a4d-8436-402d7d7ff9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452339} :answer-field/id #uuid "efec9971-12d9-5dac-9de5-e52ca41b457f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea5645c8-5c4c-53e6-a126-c5a12be2f712" :question/math-academy-id "q-97229" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨ia,ia⟩=⟨a,a⟩$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the linearity in the first argument  and the antilinearity in the second argument we have\n\n$$\n⟨ia,ia⟩=(i\\cdot \\overset{¯}{i})⟨a,a⟩=-{i}^{2}⟨a,a⟩=⟨a,a⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548355} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549116}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180f3b65-b2cb-53f6-8c04-72897f825aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452341} {:answer/id #uuid "ca765503-72af-5a62-90a8-9c3ea9e4d41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "180f3b65-b2cb-53f6-8c04-72897f825aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452341} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9da039e-c54e-5155-a392-e4ef2ae3f67c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453018} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2fb392-f964-5fb5-8969-a83bb0cb21b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452343} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb82dcb-5e7a-5feb-81a2-992930935c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2fb392-f964-5fb5-8969-a83bb0cb21b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452343} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8240300-118e-5033-a435-f2278fe983d5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6607ad8c-6b9d-5cd8-a588-8f899222623c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452345} {:answer/id #uuid "a6876d72-3057-5616-b5e0-069e3f6bc457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6876d72-3057-5616-b5e0-069e3f6bc457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452346} :answer-field/id #uuid "75d2a334-c96f-58a4-8af6-4b6abbb4289e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad8bf150-2b71-5d8f-8288-e353f02a776f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97248" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨a,-ia⟩=-i⟨a,a⟩$ for any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the antilinearity in the second argument we have\n\n$$\n⟨a,-ia⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\ne -i⟨a,a⟩\n$$\n\n \nfor any nonzero vector  $a\\in {C}^{n}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "914c5cc0-77de-5e5a-9430-0c8663b7fb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452347} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5b3124-7a98-5669-a577-2b30cc503898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5b3124-7a98-5669-a577-2b30cc503898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452348} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dc138d2-4f7c-59f8-a707-746570e3a3b8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453021} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5971c655-545f-582e-9080-64ecfc5176a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452349} {:answer/id #uuid "aae144d6-fa3b-515c-a5b3-99f9a33f4896" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5971c655-545f-582e-9080-64ecfc5176a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452349} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bcc5079-bb62-5377-8955-c42eea6e68ea" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5ada01-d7b5-56ef-a0ba-92bb91518486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452351} {:answer/id #uuid "83a11f7d-c0f2-5e90-97d1-c0f4da2784c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e5ada01-d7b5-56ef-a0ba-92bb91518486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452351} :answer-field/id #uuid "b94f1c25-e6f5-54ad-badc-528ff35eb492" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2fac0a4e-d3e8-507c-b2ff-dcb288cf0e43" :question/math-academy-id "q-97258" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n\n- **II.** $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n\n- **III.** $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\n- Statement II is false. To factor out a constant multiple from the second argument, we must change it to its complex conjugate.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445240} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445241}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3859bb5-c8b9-50e8-8eef-3af0c8937ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452353} {:answer/id #uuid "da6c7dee-677d-5806-85b1-6f0588358ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da6c7dee-677d-5806-85b1-6f0588358ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452354} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca96214-aff5-5f05-ada1-12ce791f90fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d6b082d-2576-5e1d-8655-c6e913dd6e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452355} {:answer/id #uuid "44335011-eb8f-5a0b-bb95-f537858c1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44335011-eb8f-5a0b-bb95-f537858c1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452356} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f9df55b-6d6a-5739-9911-e251543e8b83" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edba4c44-368b-51d4-98cb-48bf0ea196b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452357} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbde816-1bd9-5b75-8fc3-21d0b2f05e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edba4c44-368b-51d4-98cb-48bf0ea196b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452357} :answer-field/id #uuid "7767b767-280a-5089-ad8f-b2a80f87660b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d89a9f6-d33c-56fa-8ee8-b25b137af49f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97264" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- **III.** $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530864} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531678}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048179 :topic/id #uuid "8633737d-b07f-5466-99f0-a422586920c4" :topic/math-academy-id 3351 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Autonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0006d664-b8ff-5634-986f-5c0d4e1d7dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469884} {:answer/id #uuid "83c6dacd-fb1e-5471-803a-abd44bac5e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0006d664-b8ff-5634-986f-5c0d4e1d7dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469884} :answer-field/id #uuid "eebde2a3-3507-5638-9b44-f686205ba48d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470554} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d127a6-6075-5768-b2dc-3a7b506eee92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469886} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbf38e8-b177-50e1-9fb8-9e14988ed9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dbf38e8-b177-50e1-9fb8-9e14988ed9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469887} :answer-field/id #uuid "318d7144-ff77-5eb1-a82b-9cbffe6faa92" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "179c1b11-36a5-5f98-920b-76f389dbee6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469888} {:answer/id #uuid "d13d24a9-2960-5539-8b04-298e83c2a041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179c1b11-36a5-5f98-920b-76f389dbee6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469888} :answer-field/id #uuid "403154ae-9845-5bc7-b450-f3877f734072" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cae22cc3-a67e-53bb-bb36-eebf3af162ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-97288" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+1$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a positive slope\n- **II.** At every point along the line $y=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- **III.** At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope field has a negative slope\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=-2+1=-1<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is negative for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $-1$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,-1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-1)}=-1+1=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-1)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}=1+1=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is equal to $2$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa69f6116eba6462c4fe18f2e535d83db350f0797cf1fcd895ac6df9a4d6fd7.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048179 :topic/id #uuid "8633737d-b07f-5466-99f0-a422586920c4" :topic/math-academy-id 3351 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Autonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c98c4e-5e6c-5db9-9709-30890569a443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452359} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3c146b-f631-50f2-9adb-9d61f83920f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac3c146b-f631-50f2-9adb-9d61f83920f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452360} :answer-field/id #uuid "daff269f-d1d1-5289-befe-b825d12977f3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "403709a9-fc37-5554-8fda-4d6f19f04cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452361} {:answer/id #uuid "ab28e99f-97f5-5181-a4a0-405504e518f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab28e99f-97f5-5181-a4a0-405504e518f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452362} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ed9b4c-c797-5042-8f2e-9a28f60ee73b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ccff2a4-3b73-554e-b45f-64486b77a031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452363} {:answer/id #uuid "1c35c4e9-abab-5547-92ec-9dd9fc0194c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c35c4e9-abab-5547-92ec-9dd9fc0194c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452364} :answer-field/id #uuid "a923ebc2-6d02-50c9-9b2c-abdaaab1e550" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6350e51-d7f7-5f85-8d67-4cf2337fbb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97289" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2y$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point along the line $y=-1,$ the slope field has a negative slope\n- **II.** At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- **III.** At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope field has a positive slope" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,-1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-1)}=2(-1)=-2<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-1)$ is negative for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-1)$ is equal to $-2$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=2(0)=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}=2(1)=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is equal to $2$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69065d8e064b0fd679f059925f5445dcb2c7d037f180d3a144ee527ea408e8db.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048179 :topic/id #uuid "8633737d-b07f-5466-99f0-a422586920c4" :topic/math-academy-id 3351 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Autonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fe2147c-1f86-5070-82c6-693a696e1103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452365} {:answer/id #uuid "8130913a-e4b9-5961-8bb2-4dc3778284d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fe2147c-1f86-5070-82c6-693a696e1103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452365} :answer-field/id #uuid "74430b21-a196-5035-918b-75715c7db7e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453030} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb799ce8-a4b6-514e-8a11-ae7660dd6556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452367} {:answer/id #uuid "01da4839-d736-5a6a-96fa-bbd093b5e0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01da4839-d736-5a6a-96fa-bbd093b5e0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452368} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7a140d-7cac-55ba-b161-15343ea5e8af" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9362a2a-195c-51c4-9dcb-4faea3cf0a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452369} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e47bdf-4d9d-5986-9ca5-4bdcc1dfc043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3e47bdf-4d9d-5986-9ca5-4bdcc1dfc043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452370} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d36bfd-8e60-5cdf-b670-ef9621ab7113" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fed752d-147f-589f-b531-b8f9d3875529" :question/math-academy-id "q-97291" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a negative slope\n- **II.** At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- **III.** At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope field has a positive slope" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=(-2)^{2}=4>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $4$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=(0)^{2}=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}=(1)^{2}=1>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is equal to $1$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/0c/0c6e2e486ae770bc99ef9fe41f02d224de65119ade910d303ad3f57f12e8d84b.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048179 :topic/id #uuid "8633737d-b07f-5466-99f0-a422586920c4" :topic/math-academy-id 3351 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Autonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154f9c55-fa06-5edc-aa18-dcf55a6ec314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452371} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a78ed1-2956-5b34-8509-13f418923165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a78ed1-2956-5b34-8509-13f418923165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452372} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1648c6f-4f1e-5ed9-aa05-a613a04e751a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc85e73-9df1-57c0-bd7b-389d4617ae8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452373} {:answer/id #uuid "f734c67f-ee97-507e-b57a-0c8c7f7496f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f734c67f-ee97-507e-b57a-0c8c7f7496f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452374} :answer-field/id #uuid "222d103d-37b8-52b9-b140-a84819683bf4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec0ed88a-36c1-5f7c-a9a1-7f904f629949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452375} {:answer/id #uuid "450a5377-249f-51c2-b1c4-d8e425a5860d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "450a5377-249f-51c2-b1c4-d8e425a5860d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452376} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea99e78-c93a-57d3-af14-62e1ba23e473" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c547f26-e43a-5839-bf5f-d8b1c5da69a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97292" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point along the line $y=-1,$ the slope of the slope field does not vary\n- **II.** At every point along the line $x=1,$ the slope of the slope field varies\n- **III.** At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,-1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-1)}=-(-1)^{2}=-1,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-1)$ is equal to $-1$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(1,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,y)}=-{y}^{2},\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(1,y)$ depends on $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=-(0)^{2}=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"\n\nWe can use the information given by the true statements to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/27/272427db87d74e3d4ae09dc69b7add53e8def9ead184a1ab90afc99fc0a7628e.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be7f699-9974-5201-8e47-accce63d5602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452377} {:answer/id #uuid "19455cdc-333a-5561-bab6-00ec79218d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9be7f699-9974-5201-8e47-accce63d5602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452377} :answer-field/id #uuid "5582b199-c5bf-5709-9377-1286b2173eaa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d491e753-0d53-5704-b768-2cde723d0d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452379} {:answer/id #uuid "fda07ff9-ba7b-5689-857e-ab9f1cd84952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda07ff9-ba7b-5689-857e-ab9f1cd84952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452380} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3df9eb2-97cb-5280-9fe0-ea7eec6cc287" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1794a0-b828-5e06-b8cc-54a54ad72949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452381} {:answer/id #uuid "b15deefa-87b8-5a6a-89b0-4f57df04b649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d1794a0-b828-5e06-b8cc-54a54ad72949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452381} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b86e18f-b4ac-528d-b5e3-1bc836241d7d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "354bca31-ea8a-5e1d-a896-d3e34e677d11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97296" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n\n- **II.** $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-ib⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n\n- **III.** There is vector $a\\in {C}^{n}$ such that  $⟨a,a⟩<0$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. A complex number is equal to its conjugate if and only if it is a real number. The inner product over $C$  is a complex number in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ib⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false.  The inner product over $C$ is positive-definite. So, for any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445240} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445244} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530864} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531713}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8dac23-f647-5deb-86a4-621fd31c1d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452383} {:answer/id #uuid "6e03bff6-a5ff-50e6-9218-131abe220023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e03bff6-a5ff-50e6-9218-131abe220023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452384} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9c2f28-e2b4-59be-ae0d-5cc27032c71a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d384c3-9e31-5d82-9ef2-635c223f8ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452385} {:answer/id #uuid "140655d4-6272-5a39-a781-b9c1417ede63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d384c3-9e31-5d82-9ef2-635c223f8ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452385} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50118f5-3a96-5d52-9890-18e710ce477d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1709b99a-c168-519e-a774-35d4b3d2341e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452387} {:answer/id #uuid "f478c422-93f8-5410-a67c-fea2ce11d298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f478c422-93f8-5410-a67c-fea2ce11d298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452388} :answer-field/id #uuid "86902f25-2bcd-545b-9255-65d88893b5e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8247f7d2-00cd-54b9-9bd1-43c13383de3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97303" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨b,a⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨-ia,b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. A complex  inner product is linear  in the first argument,  so we have \n\n$$\n⟨-ia,b⟩=-i⟨a,b⟩\\ne i⟨a,b⟩,\n$$\n\nin general.\n\n- Statement III is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"} :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530864} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531711}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097 :topic/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid 