)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y=-3$ is a node.\n\nII. $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nIII. $y=2$ is a source.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/36/362ffe8871efa8dc597708b039fa766c3603777ba12460e84d9af1fc39800288.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-3$ is a node.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 8" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435898} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435934} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048131 :topic/id #uuid "81e52842-e868-5110-93ce-65b6024b5770" :topic/math-academy-id 2533 :topic/title "Classifying Equilibrium Solutions of First-Order ODEs"} :activity/title "Classifying Equilibrium Solutions of First-Order ODEs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562924} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563765}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title 