-56be-805f-f8a4da6ba9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470953} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a1e2d7d-bec5-5fe7-8248-ae4746a2c58c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d4a2162-ef8c-55f6-9a59-3237823f3b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125660" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({e}^{x+y}-4x)\\,i+({e}^{x+y}+6y)\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $F$ is **not** conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement III is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"} :activity/title "Circulation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547301} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548159}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81170187-aa6e-5bfa-b16b-ae1c857eaa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453312} {:answer/id #uuid "e642b50f-fc15-598c-8734-9ce786c97378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e642b50f-fc15-598c-8734-9ce786c97378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453313} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6c1faa-915a-575a-9ae6-ee5d18d7b44c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f5f792-942f-538c-a2b1-487c714d1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453314} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f7fbd1-2c63-5201-8723-39a46c7046c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f5f792-942f-538c-a2b1-487c714d1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453314} :answer-field/id #u