d $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9c554b-d6e3-52ed-b916-eff4bbabf9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453318} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dc769-6e03-5a92-8482-5168690a775a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dc769-6e03-5a92-8482-5168690a775a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453319} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bdfca1a-584e-538d-a8d3-3072dca98494" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4334bdd4-9c1f-50e7-8b9c-07c6d8fdca99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453320} {:answer/id #uuid "7df7187a-4d59-587f-93cc-9c009e0929d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df7187a-4d59-587f-93cc-9c009e0929d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453321} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d8d4b7-46b3-5bcb-ac17-298d14c20437" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee87d2cb-ee2e-5a8d-a70b-3564d5aa2f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453322} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfdf8ab-48c2-5a0e-a0a2-baf7ed4dcfc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdfdf8ab-48c2-5a0e-a0a2-baf7ed4dcfc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453323} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8edc981-6f69-524a-a43a-a0ba1b3c3778" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12c57671-3717-5693-b7e2-6cfc6da6f16d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125662" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(x{e}^{y}+5)\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{y}}{2}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative\n- **II.** ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=x{e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II and III are true. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Continuous Random Variables Given in Context" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049638 :topic/id #uuid "0748b9c2-fae7-5522-9655-db9e6f1d50c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1347 :topic/title "Probability Density Functions of Continuous Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65dd1653-3254-5f54-870f-f09d3ba1ccce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470955} {:answer/id #uuid "753fef14-5e64-5c52-886f-6fd1b9061dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "753fef14-5e64-5c52-886f-6fd1b9061dac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470956} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea35560f-215e-5a98-b654-d492c18033bf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc980ec6-4340-5927-99df-cd904a37231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470957} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9f5fbd-47f6-5c2e-8776-142614bcc7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc980ec6-4340-5927-99df-cd904a37231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470957} :answer-field/id #uuid "79896b85-8f49-55ab-b573-212de9b851a0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dd16a5b-38ff-549d-aa7f-f993bf6dd978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470959} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa23451-791e-5d35-afbb-1a118e5a528b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aa23451-791e-5d35-afbb-1a118e5a528b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470960} :answer-field/id #uuid "41e61440-7118-529e-bc48-6e375d91fabd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ab10e57-92ba-5362-9127-1131b20d7150" :question/math-academy-id "q-126051" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n- **I.** The quantity of fat, in grams per kilogram, in a sausage\n- **II.** The number of points out of $50$ that a student gets in a math test\n- **III.** The weight, measured  in kilograms, of a randomly selected seventeen-year-old student\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,1\\,000].$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,3,…,50,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement III describes a  continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050567 :topic/id #uuid "54747772-1cac-572e-9b8f-be3a6c8abe45" :topic/math-academy-id 2198 :topic/title "Using Green's Theorem to Calculate Area"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae6522b-d021-5d59-8cd6-f5304bdd55ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437758} {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8414dbe-30d0-5384-b8c5-62cc6232e458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437759} :answer-field/id #uuid "748fe4bc-f5a7-5f6e-a198-2ec4af1a9fb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} {:answer/id #uuid "1f174d76-4611-5f5a-bb29-5066e184e17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fcddd5-827b-5326-b25a-877e35a9d273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437760} :answer-field/id #uuid "93da9704-e1a5-5081-8553-7cd992df06d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffa29f7-20b1-5b11-99da-52f6143261ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437762} {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4926ca4-8616-57f1-a942-8235f95a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437763} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c21734-8e5a-535d-ada3-66000108f100" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5aefc1-27f1-5c4b-be31-6e2e9699a7da" :question/math-academy-id "q-126560" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{y}{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{x}{2}$\n- **II.** $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area.  In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050567 :topic/id #uuid "54747772-1cac-572e-9b8f-be3a6c8abe45" :topic/math-academy-id 2198 :topic/title "Using Green's Theorem to Calculate Area"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f3c085-feb8-513f-add4-66aa98bd17ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437764} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fe0d2ca-9939-5556-96db-9df34ee271ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437765} :answer-field/id #uuid "18de6163-4953-583e-b212-b0337c772ec5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} {:answer/id #uuid "218378a4-fbcd-5e98-8eff-a70c74b13433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dc332b0-9c6c-52fb-9960-0a34a7b12892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437766} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d6dd72a-3e01-555e-a264-373480cb3397" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8116a580-f40c-5f87-8318-cb566921d6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437768} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebb283d0-c938-5e90-8f21-2d9015525c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437769} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cf9841-fb2d-5f21-9260-8a5cc7b8a700" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5decc408-adb2-55a3-accb-8195735690a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-126571" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,y⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050567 :topic/id #uuid "54747772-1cac-572e-9b8f-be3a6c8abe45" :topic/math-academy-id 2198 :topic/title "Using Green's Theorem to Calculate Area"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} {:answer/id #uuid "de7792c1-6264-5b26-a11b-f266fd2ffbf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5314efe-6d3d-5874-a4e8-e3bb02359b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437782} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9aea2b-8ded-5e68-bdc8-80f01907fab2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} {:answer/id #uuid "cca9abd2-28b1-50b1-a0d7-213e565a3526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3e2c30-0387-56e6-9017-184fe08df055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf91cf4-1adf-55a1-bef6-7fd579465082" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e066b5f-ee40-571e-9d64-c19fe307ffad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437786} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbbfdda-889f-50b7-8d61-3c68b8acb082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437787} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dea6355-4414-5031-bdce-266f0e70af29" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a19e15dc-6544-52f9-9d54-2c5e5b2885d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126577" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,y⟩$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{7},\\,\\frac{6x}{7}⟩$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}-{e}^{-y},\\,x{e}^{-y}+x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{7}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{6}{7},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{5}{7}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{-y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{-y}+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159 :topic/id #uuid "df2bac79-2def-521c-b3f0-baba942d57fa" :topic/math-academy-id 1771 :topic/title "Basic Properties of Determinants"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50fda18-64bf-56e5-8e3c-c238feedb593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453356} {:answer/id #uuid "33b1e846-122d-598e-a81d-c96a868efe86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b50fda18-64bf-56e5-8e3c-c238feedb593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/iden