71165} :answer-field/id #uuid "498b9449-b183-59dc-8461-4984778c1d56" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0311da7-2e05-528f-8234-394bbb366e6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-174352" :question/problem "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n\nI. $\\{3,4,5\\}$ and $\\{6,7,8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{-4,-3,-2\\}$ and $\\{2,3,4\\}$\n\nIII. $[-3,0]$ and $[0,3]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{3,4,5\\}\\cap \\{6,7,8\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair II is also disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n\\{-4,-3,-2\\}\\cap \\{2,3,4\\}=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Pair III is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n[-3,0]\\cap [0,3]=\\{0\\}\\ne ∅\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048864 :topic/id #uuid "c788c893-5c00-5b28-be4c-bd65dc3ed101" :topic/math-academy-id 2789 :topic/title "Disjoint Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe7defe-a71a-57a7-8f21-270ae5e67822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471167} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb77cda-2863-59bc-a98b-6353a74f96f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fe7defe-a71a-57a7-8f21-270ae5e67822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471167} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed05bf51-1485-58e0-ac84-9569b4a15493" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f661720-0b47-565b-975f-93a482a5a9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471169} {:answer/id #uuid "fff11aaa-bc23-5831-803a-be91945ed479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f661720-0b47-565b-975f-93a482a5a9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471169} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d8eb5c9-3745-5f9b-a205-883c5ebbc615" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a4b793-b776-5ab6-b915-8af840ed0686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471171} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c315a2-05c9-5833-bb8c-a1ecefc4aac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5c315a2-05c9-5833-bb8c-a1ecefc4aac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471172} :answer-field/id #uuid "310a3c1c-dfb5-512f-9af7-149fd6efdbae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3022ca1-a812-5c84-9bb2-a207567a5c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-174355" :question/problem "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n- **I.** ${2,4,8}$ and ${8,16,32}$\n- **II.** ${1,e,\\pi }$ and ${0,1,2}$\n- **III.** $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(0,\\infty )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n{2,4,8}\\cap {8,16,32}={8}\\ne ∅\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Pair II is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n{1,e,\\pi }\\cap {0,1,2}={1}\\ne ∅\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Pair III is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0)\\cap (0,\\infty )=∅\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048864 :topic/id #uuid "c788c893-5c00-5b28-be4c-bd65dc3ed101" :topic/math-academy-id 2789 :topic/title "Disjoint Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "507029b2-3fd6-5034-954e-ed66a85df293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453550} {:answer/id #uuid "ec635114-5312-531c-b42d-c4da392fc908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec635114-5312-531c-b42d-c4da392fc908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453551} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf8c311-bd7f-5dcd-beb1-b22999665db3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2521d433-2bfd-5cfe-b421-88df61ee9eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453552} {:answer/id #uuid "3be4d17a-b21b-5691-8480-f76f1fd3d84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3be4d17a-b21b-5691-8480-f76f1fd3d84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453553} :answer-field/id #uuid "571a08e4-e818-55ff-ab90-ce0244a0e22e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b449082-a63e-5d27-8106-c928b763eafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453554} {:answer/id #uuid "04397924-fb85-5900-ac82-9ea80a05d4f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04397924-fb85-5900-ac82-9ea80a05d4f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453555} :answer-field/id #uuid "11bb38d2-8621-5039-ae02-1f0331b902d0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fbffaaa-23d8-507a-8897-e781a41c0406" :question/math-academy-id "q-174356" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={n\\in N∣2n+1<9},\\,B={n\\in N∣n\\ge 4}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A={1,2,3}$\n- **II.** $A\\cap B=∅$\n- **III.** $A$ and $B$ are disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the elements of $A$ are positive integers that satisfy the inequality \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+1 & <9 \\\\ 2n & <8 \\\\ n & <4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={n\\in N∣2n+1<9} \\\\  & ={n\\in N∣n<4} \\\\  & ={1,2,3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={n\\in N∣n\\ge 4} \\\\  & ={4,5,6,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B={1,2,3}\\cap {4,5,6,…}=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048864 :topic/id #uuid "c788c893-5c00-5b28-be4c-bd65dc3ed101" :topic/math-academy-id 2789 :topic/title "Disjoint Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba140682-0e8f-5aca-8de3-cdd0b1bc2c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453556} {:answer/id #uuid "396921ad-aa40-5aaa-884e-027a229971c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :a