b/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e6d5c0d-f5b8-5d41-acfe-dd83480488ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-174369" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={2n∣n\\in N},\\,B={{2}^{n}∣n\\in N}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B={2,4,8,16,…}$\n- **II.** $A\\cap B=∅$\n- **III.** $A$ and $B$ are disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={{2}^{n}∣n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,16,…}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={2n∣n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cap B & ={2,4,6,8,…}\\text{ }\\cap {2,4,8,16,…} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,…} \\\\  & \\ne ∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the intersection is not empty, the two sets are not disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048864 :topic/id #uuid "c788c893-5c00-5b28-be4c-bd65dc3ed101" :topic/math-academy-id 2789 :topic/title "Disjoint Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7bb5f41-fcb4-5d02-91d0-f31e1c3de7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453562} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f4a44e-d637-52cf-a887-73cc0d97a0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218