III.** $¬X∧Y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧Y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬X∧Y$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050360 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250 :topic/title "Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382b0e40-0b72-5c5c-9d94-193493c39204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471687} {:answer/id #uuid "ce73943b-79af-5cb9-8def-b3e711d8e0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382b0e40-0b72-5c5c-9d94-193493c39204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471687} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb80344b-80bc-5f25-8430-2d5d6bd787bb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120d3451-1808-58bd-a146-10d1068008fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471689} {:answer/id #uuid "161c51b2-8820-5a19-8c55-8c44271bd04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "161c51b2-8820-5a19-8c55-8c44271bd04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471690} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0a9c54-4abd-51b2-8613-c8fac1cc2414" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "677cd23a-a88e-5e97-a475-ca256aa1f1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471691} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dfca88-d58d-5326-958d-bb7cbc86b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dfca88-d58d-5326-958d-bb7cbc86b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471692} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca18faec-5ae3-50f0-af6d-fa9045deca1b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28c545f7-d207-5c17-a488-3a5f17bee359" :question/math-academy-id "q-82071" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** **If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $8$ is a prime number.\n- **II.** **If** $8$ is an even number, **then** $2$ is an even number.\n- **III.** **If** $8$ is a prime number, **then** $2$ is an even number.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$8$ is a prime number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$8$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$8$ is a prime number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050360 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250 :topic/title "Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ebdb5b2-a035-5e73-b3a5-fea90ac2c5f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471693} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcf4f12-388d-5ee8-afa1-ccb824f1a67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcf4f12-388d-5ee8-afa1-ccb824f1a67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va