17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e834c31-c35d-57df-a0ce-02370148728a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82089" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** **If** $2+3<4,$ **then** $1+5<8.$\n- **II.** **If** $1+5<8,$ **then** $2+3<4.$\n- **III.** **If** $1+5<4,$ **then** $2+3<8.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent $2+3<4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent $1+5<8$ is true, and the consequent $2+3<4$ is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $1+5<4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050777 :topic/id #uuid "65e4f73e-43a8-5089-914d-135e7396b995" :topic/math-academy-id 2821 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c290820-a094-51ac-84b5-47702a109966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471771} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9124fe-1470-5337-aa89-5154e8ad7638" :answer/type {:db/id 