ld/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4951a3e-3ef9-5319-bbf9-d2c571b3026e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86684" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n- **I.** $¬(¬X∧¬Y)$\n- **II.** $¬X∨¬Y$\n- **III.** $¬(X∧Y)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∧Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∨¬Y$ and $¬(X∧Y)$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]
